{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"LineString","coordinates":[[19,70],[0,64],[-20,50],[-45,30],[-61,16.8]]},"properties":{"name":"Humpback whale · North Atlantic to the West Indies","Leg":"Migration route"}}
{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-68.5,42.3]},"properties":{"name":"Humpback whale · North Atlantic to the West Indies","Species":"Humpback whale (Megaptera novaeangliae)","Population":"West Indies DPS","Feeding / summer ground":"Gulf of Maine, Newfoundland, West Greenland, Iceland, Norway","Breeding / winter ground":"Silver & Navidad Banks (Dominican Rep.), Lesser Antilles","Distance (km)":"~2,800 (Maine) to ~8,000 (Norway)","Timing":"Feed May–Nov; breed Jan–Apr, peak Feb–Mar","Abundance":"~12,000","Status":"Not at risk","Confidence":"Well documented","Notes":"Nearly all western North Atlantic humpbacks converge on the Caribbean. Photo-ID has matched whales from northern Norway to Guadeloupe."}}
