{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-63,-64.5]},"properties":{"name":"Humpback whale · Antarctic Peninsula to Colombia & Panama","Species":"Humpback whale (Megaptera novaeangliae)","Population":"Breeding Stock G (SE Pacific)","Feeding / summer ground":"Western Antarctic Peninsula, Strait of Magellan","Breeding / winter ground":"Ecuador, Colombia, Panama, Costa Rica","Distance (km)":"Up to ~8,300 one way","Timing":"Feed Dec–Apr; breed Jun–Oct","Abundance":"~10,000+","Status":"Recovering","Confidence":"Well documented","Notes":"Among the longest regular migrations of any mammal. These whales cross the equator, so Central America hosts humpbacks from both hemispheres in different seasons."}}
{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"LineString","coordinates":[[-34,-56],[-37,-45],[-37,-30],[-38.4,-18]]},"properties":{"name":"Humpback whale · South Georgia to Abrolhos Bank","Leg":"Migration route"}}
{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-34,-56]},"properties":{"name":"Humpback whale · South Georgia to Abrolhos Bank","Species":"Humpback whale (Megaptera novaeangliae)","Population":"Breeding Stock A (Brazil)","Feeding / summer ground":"South Georgia & South Sandwich Islands","Breeding / winter ground":"Abrolhos Bank, Bahia, Brazil","Distance (km)":"~4,000 one way","Timing":"Feed Dec–Apr; breed Jul–Nov","Abundance":"~25,000","Status":"Largely recovered","Confidence":"Well documented","Notes":"Reduced to a few hundred animals by whaling, this population is now estimated at over 90% of its pre-whaling size."}}
{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"LineString","coordinates":[[5,-60],[10,-45],[11,-30],[10,-15],[8.5,-1]]},"properties":{"name":"Humpback whale · Southern Ocean to Gabon","Leg":"Migration route"}}
{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[5,-60]},"properties":{"name":"Humpback whale · Southern Ocean to Gabon","Species":"Humpback whale (Megaptera novaeangliae)","Population":"Breeding Stock B (SE Atlantic)","Feeding / summer ground":"Southern Ocean near Bouvet Island","Breeding / winter ground":"Gabon, Congo, Angola coast","Distance (km)":"~5,000–6,500 one way","Timing":"Feed Dec–Apr; breed Jul–Oct","Abundance":"Several thousand","Status":"Recovering","Confidence":"Partly known","Notes":"Satellite tags show whales travelling south along the Namibian coast and then far offshore; the Antarctic feeding area is broadly located but not well defined."}}
