{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-170,-66]},"properties":{"name":"Humpback whale · Antarctica to Tonga, New Caledonia & French Polynesia","Species":"Humpback whale (Megaptera novaeangliae)","Population":"Breeding Stocks E2, E3, F (Oceania)","Feeding / summer ground":"Southern Ocean, Ross Sea sector","Breeding / winter ground":"Tonga (Vavaʻu), New Caledonia, French Polynesia, Cook Is.","Distance (km)":"~5,000–6,000 one way","Timing":"Breed Jul–Oct","Abundance":"A few thousand","Status":"Endangered (IUCN, Oceania subpop.)","Confidence":"Partly known","Notes":"Island groups are partly isolated from one another; recovery is slower than off Australia. Antarctic destinations come from a handful of tags and photo matches."}}
