{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-168,68]},"properties":{"name":"Gray whale · Arctic to the Baja lagoons","Species":"Gray whale (Eschrichtius robustus)","Population":"Eastern North Pacific","Feeding / summer ground":"Chukchi & northern Bering Seas","Breeding / winter ground":"Laguna Ojo de Liebre, San Ignacio, Bahía Magdalena","Distance (km)":"8,000–10,000 one way; 16,000–20,000 round trip","Timing":"South Oct–Feb; calving Jan–Mar; north Feb–May, mothers & calves last","Abundance":"~13,000 (2024–25)","Status":"Least concern; recent sharp decline","Confidence":"Well documented","Notes":"A largely coastal route, which makes it the most watched whale migration in the world. Numbers dropped by about half after 2016 during an unusual mortality event linked to poor Arctic feeding."}}
