{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[143.5,52.8]},"properties":{"name":"Gray whale · Sakhalin to Baja (and Asia)","Species":"Gray whale (Eschrichtius robustus)","Population":"Western North Pacific","Feeding / summer ground":"Piltun Lagoon, NE Sakhalin Island","Breeding / winter ground":"Baja California (tagged whales); South China Sea (historical)","Distance (km)":"~11,000 one way","Timing":"Feed Jun–Nov off Sakhalin; winter destination varies","Abundance":"~300 on the Sakhalin feeding ground","Status":"Endangered (IUCN)","Confidence":"Partly known","Notes":"A tagged female named Varvara swam 22,511 km round trip from Sakhalin to Baja and back in 172 days, the longest mammal migration then recorded. Some western whales may still winter off Asia, the dashed historical route."}}
