{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[140.5,-38.6]},"properties":{"name":"Blue whale · Southern Australia to the Banda Sea","Species":"Blue whale (Balaenoptera musculus)","Population":"Pygmy blue whale (E. Indian Ocean)","Feeding / summer ground":"Bonney Upwelling (Vic/SA) & Perth Canyon (WA)","Breeding / winter ground":"Banda Sea & eastern Indonesia","Distance (km)":"~3,000–5,000 one way","Timing":"Feed Nov–May off southern Australia; north Apr–Jun along the WA coast","Abundance":"Not well estimated","Status":"Endangered (species)","Confidence":"Well documented","Notes":"Satellite tags showed whales hugging the Western Australian shelf edge before turning into Indonesian waters, raising concern about shipping and seismic surveys on the corridor."}}
