{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-74.8,-43.5]},"properties":{"name":"Blue whale · Chilean Patagonia to Galápagos","Species":"Blue whale (Balaenoptera musculus)","Population":"Chilean blue whale","Feeding / summer ground":"Corcovado Gulf & Chiloé, Patagonia","Breeding / winter ground":"Eastern tropical Pacific near Galápagos & Peru","Distance (km)":"~4,500 one way","Timing":"Feed Jan–May in Patagonia; winter in the tropics","Abundance":"Not well estimated","Status":"Endangered (species)","Confidence":"Well documented","Notes":"Tagging confirmed the link between Patagonian fjords and equatorial waters; the Patagonian feeding area overlaps heavy salmon-farm vessel traffic."}}
