{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-64,48]},"properties":{"name":"Right whale · Gulf of St Lawrence to Georgia & Florida","Species":"Right whale (Eubalaena glacialis / E. australis)","Population":"North Atlantic right whale","Feeding / summer ground":"Gulf of St Lawrence, Bay of Fundy, Cape Cod Bay","Breeding / winter ground":"Coastal Georgia & NE Florida (calving)","Distance (km)":"~2,000–2,500 one way","Timing":"Calving Dec–Mar; Cape Cod Bay Feb–Apr; Gulf of St Lawrence Jun–Oct","Abundance":"~370","Status":"Critically endangered","Confidence":"Well documented","Notes":"Only pregnant females and some juveniles make the full run to the calving grounds. Since about 2015 many whales have shifted summer feeding into the Gulf of St Lawrence, following their copepod prey."}}
