{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-124,70.6]},"properties":{"name":"Bowhead whale · Bering Sea to the Beaufort Sea","Species":"Bowhead whale (Balaena mysticetus)","Population":"Bering–Chukchi–Beaufort","Feeding / summer ground":"Eastern Beaufort Sea & Amundsen Gulf (summer)","Breeding / winter ground":"Bering Sea pack ice (winter)","Distance (km)":"~3,000 one way","Timing":"Spring north Apr–Jun past Point Barrow; fall west Sep–Nov along Chukotka","Abundance":"~12,500","Status":"Least concern; Alaska Native subsistence hunt","Confidence":"Well documented","Notes":"A loop migration: whales travel east through nearshore leads in spring and return west across the Chukchi Sea in autumn. Bowheads can live more than 200 years."}}
{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"LineString","coordinates":[[-89.5,73.5],[-80,74.3],[-72,72.5],[-67,70],[-53,68.9],[-61,64],[-70,61.5]]},"properties":{"name":"Bowhead whale · Hudson Strait to Baffin Bay","Leg":"Migration route"}}
{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-89.5,73.5]},"properties":{"name":"Bowhead whale · Hudson Strait to Baffin Bay","Species":"Bowhead whale (Balaena mysticetus)","Population":"Eastern Canada–West Greenland","Feeding / summer ground":"Isabella Bay, Lancaster Sound, Prince Regent Inlet","Breeding / winter ground":"Hudson Strait & Davis Strait pack ice; Disko Bay in spring","Distance (km)":"~2,000–2,500 one way","Timing":"Disko Bay Mar–May; high Arctic summer; winter in Hudson Strait","Abundance":"~6,000–7,000","Status":"Least concern (recovering)","Confidence":"Well documented","Notes":"Satellite tracking in Greenland and Canada showed these two once-separate hunting stocks are a single population moving around Baffin Bay."}}
