{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-93.9,59]},"properties":{"name":"Beluga whale · Hudson Strait to Churchill estuaries","Species":"Beluga whale (Delphinapterus leucas)","Population":"Western Hudson Bay beluga","Feeding / summer ground":"Churchill, Nelson & Seal River estuaries (summer)","Breeding / winter ground":"Hudson Strait & Labrador Sea ice edge (winter)","Distance (km)":"~1,500–2,000 one way","Timing":"Estuaries Jul–Aug; leave Sep–Oct","Abundance":"~55,000","Status":"Least concern","Confidence":"Well documented","Notes":"The largest beluga population in the world. Thousands gather in warm, shallow river mouths in summer, likely for moulting and calf protection."}}
{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"LineString","coordinates":[[-79.5,72.7],[-74.5,72.6],[-64,72.5],[-58,69.5]]},"properties":{"name":"Narwhal whale · Eclipse Sound to Baffin Bay","Leg":"Migration route"}}
{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-79.5,72.7]},"properties":{"name":"Narwhal whale · Eclipse Sound to Baffin Bay","Species":"Narwhal whale (Monodon monoceros)","Population":"Baffin Bay narwhal","Feeding / summer ground":"Eclipse Sound, Admiralty Inlet, Lancaster Sound (summer)","Breeding / winter ground":"Dense pack ice of central Baffin Bay & Davis Strait (winter)","Distance (km)":"~1,000–1,700 one way","Timing":"Fjords Jul–Aug; migrate Sep–Oct; winter Nov–Apr under the ice","Abundance":"Tens of thousands","Status":"Least concern","Confidence":"Well documented","Notes":"In winter narwhals dive more than 1,500 m beneath heavy pack ice to feed on Greenland halibut; summer fjords overlap increasing ship traffic."}}
